# Netlify custom headers.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file is intentionally credential-free. It used to contain
# a literal Basic-Auth rule with placeholder credentials
# (paul:REPLACE_ME_1, colleague2:REPLACE_ME_2, colleague3:REPLACE_ME_3) —
# committed straight into the repo, which means every clone/zip shipped a
# documented, guessable access gate. See docs/dev-notes and
# SECURITY_AND_KEYS.md ("Netlify Basic-Auth credentials").
#
# The real Basic-Auth rule is now generated at build time by
# scripts/generate-headers.mjs (runs automatically as part of `npm run
# build`, after `vite build`) from the NETLIFY_BASIC_AUTH_CREDENTIALS
# environment variable, and written into dist/_headers only — dist/ is
# gitignored and never committed.
#
# Running `vite dev` or `vite preview` directly (bypassing `npm run
# build`) will NOT apply Basic-Auth; that's expected for local
# development, not a bug.
